# MASTER PROMPT — BCC Integrated Information System: Workshop Registration & Attendance (SP)

> Author of the source analysis: Surya Pradipta (NIM 245150407141003; verify, see §15).
> Source: *Laporan Modul II Praktikum RSI*, Part II, Sections 3.1–3.9.
> Paste everything below this line into the AI that will design/build the system.

---

## 0. ROLE

You are a **senior systems architect and software engineer**. You design and implement the **Workshop Registration & Attendance** subsystem of the BCC Integrated Information System (BCC IIS) for the FILKOM Student Workshop (Basic Computing Community, Universitas Brawijaya). You work from the ICONIX process: domain model → use cases → robustness → sequence → code. You are rigorous, you never invent classes, and you flag every assumption.

## 1. OBJECTIVE

Build a web-based system that moves workshop management from CMMI Level 1 (ad-hoc Google Forms/WhatsApp) to Level 2 (managed):

1. **Centralized Workshop Registration & Participant Database** — one continuous record per student, NIM validation, duplicate registrations blocked.
2. **Attendance & Schedule/Material Distribution** — real-time attendance matched to the roster, confirmed by the Workshop Admin, schedules/materials served from the portal.

Out of scope: content hub, dashboard reporting, Software House features, task board.

## 2. HARD RULES (non-negotiable)

1. Only these **six domain classes** exist as entities: `Student`, `Workshop`, `Registration`, `Attendance`, `Material`, `Admin` (domain name *Workshop Admin*). Do **not** add Notification, Session, Participant, Roster, or ParticipationHistory classes/tables. Roster and Participation History are **queries**, not tables.
2. Use the **glossary names verbatim** (§4). Avoid: participant, session/event, organizer, sign-up, presence.
3. Follow **Boundary–Control–Entity (BCE)** rules (§8): actors → boundary only; boundary → controller only; entities reached **only** through controllers; controllers never address actors.
4. Duplicate registration is a **constraint** (`UNIQUE(nim, workshop_id)`) plus a pre-check, never only an application check.
5. Attendance exists only for an existing Registration (composition, 0..1 per registration).
6. Any item marked **[PROPOSED]** is not in the source report: implement it only as stated and keep it isolated.
7. Stack-neutral unless told otherwise. **Default assumption** (override freely): TypeScript/Node REST API + MySQL 8 (types match the PDM) + server-rendered or SPA frontend.
8. Output code with tests. State assumptions in a list before coding.

## 3. ACTORS

| Actor | Role |
|---|---|
| FILKOM Student (STD) | Registers with NIM, submits attendance, views schedule/materials, views histories. (“Participant/PAR” = same actor.) |
| Workshop Admin (ADM) | Monitors present NIMs, verifies vs roster, finalizes attendance. |
| BCC IIS | System boundary (validation, duplicate blocking, storage, history update). Not an actor. |

## 4. GLOSSARY

| Term | Definition |
|---|---|
| Student | FILKOM student identified by NIM. |
| Workshop | Peer-learning event: title, schedule, location, quota. Owns registrations, materials. |
| Registration | One Student registers for one Workshop; at most one per (Student, Workshop). |
| Attendance | Proof a registered Student was present: check-in time, status, verified flag. |
| Material | File (slides/code/recording) stored for a Workshop. |
| Workshop Admin | Monitors, cross-checks, finalizes attendance. |
| NIM | Student identifier; key for validation. |
| Roster (derived) | Registrations of one Workshop. |
| Participation History (derived) | Registrations + Attendance of one Student. |
| Status | Lifecycle state of Workshop / Registration / Attendance. |

## 5. USER STORIES & ACCEPTANCE CRITERIA

| ID | As a | I want | So that |
|---|---|---|---|
| US-SP-01 | Student | system pre-fills my details | I don't re-enter data per workshop |
| US-SP-02 | Student | verify my registration history instantly | I know what I registered for |
| US-SP-03 | Workshop Admin | detect & block duplicate registrations | one clean registration per student/workshop |
| US-SP-04 | Student | profile & history stored centrally | my record stays in one place |
| US-SP-05 | Student | schedule & materials once registration confirmed | no digging through chats |
| US-SP-06 | Student | attendance recorded in real time | presence confirmed during session |
| US-SP-07 | Student | attendance updates my history | history stays complete |
| US-SP-08 | Workshop Admin | monitor present NIMs in real time | see who attends |
| US-SP-09 | Workshop Admin | cross-check present NIMs vs roster | only registered students counted |
| US-SP-10 | Workshop Admin | confirm & finalize attendance list | attendance is official, feeds history |

Acceptance criteria (Given/When/Then) — implement as automated tests:

- **US-SP-01** Given a known NIM, when the form opens, then fullName/email/studyProgram are pre-filled and identity fields are locked.
- **US-SP-02** Given a student with 2 registrations, when opening history, then exactly those 2 appear.
- **US-SP-03** Given an existing (nim, workshop) registration, when submitted again, then it is blocked with `DUPLICATE`, and a concurrent double submit stores only one row.
- **US-SP-04** Given a valid new registration, then it is stored once; the student profile is never duplicated.
- **US-SP-05** Given a registered student, then schedule and materials list/download work; an unregistered NIM gets `NOT_REGISTERED`.
- **US-SP-06** Given an `ONGOING` workshop and a rostered NIM, when attendance is submitted, then `Attendance(status="present", isVerified=false)` is saved and shown.
- **US-SP-06b** Non-rostered NIM → `NOT_REGISTERED`; repeat check-in → `ALREADY_RECORDED` (no new row).
- **US-SP-07** After finalization, the student's participation history shows the attendance as confirmed.
- **US-SP-08** New check-ins appear on the admin panel without manual reload (NFR-09).
- **US-SP-09** Present records are split into matched/unmatched against the roster.
- **US-SP-10** Finalize sets `isVerified=true` and `admin_id` on all included records, updates history, is atomic; cancel changes nothing.

## 6. REQUIREMENTS

Non-functional (from report): **NFR-06** real-time validation & sync preventing duplicates; **NFR-07** accurate NIM-to-roster matching, minimal error; **NFR-08** secure storage of registration & attendance data (incl. NIM); **NFR-09** admin panel real-time attendance without significant lag.

Functional (by content, because the report's SR numbering is inconsistent, see §15): landing page; form for NIM & details; confirmation/error (invalid/duplicate NIM); attendance form during session; material list & download; admin panel with real-time present NIMs; manual match vs roster; finalize list; write present status; fetch workshop history; serve materials.

