## 13. DATA MODEL (PDM) & DDL

```mermaid
erDiagram
  STUDENT ||--o{ REGISTRATION : makes
  WORKSHOP ||--o{ REGISTRATION : "is for"
  REGISTRATION ||--o| ATTENDANCE : "results in"
  ADMIN |o--o{ ATTENDANCE : confirms
  WORKSHOP ||--o{ MATERIAL : has
  STUDENT { varchar15 nim PK; varchar100 full_name; varchar100 email; varchar50 study_program }
  WORKSHOP { int workshop_id PK; varchar150 title; datetime schedule_date; varchar100 location; int quota; varchar20 status }
  REGISTRATION { int registration_id PK; varchar15 nim FK; int workshop_id FK; datetime registered_at; varchar20 status }
  ATTENDANCE { int attendance_id PK; int registration_id FK_UQ; int admin_id FK; datetime checked_in_at; varchar20 status; boolean is_verified }
  ADMIN { int admin_id PK; varchar100 full_name; varchar30 role; varchar100 email }
  MATERIAL { int material_id PK; int workshop_id FK; varchar150 title; varchar255 file_url; datetime uploaded_at }
```

```sql
CREATE TABLE student (nim VARCHAR(15) PRIMARY KEY, full_name VARCHAR(100) NOT NULL, email VARCHAR(100) NOT NULL, study_program VARCHAR(50) NOT NULL);
CREATE TABLE workshop (workshop_id INT AUTO_INCREMENT PRIMARY KEY, title VARCHAR(150) NOT NULL, schedule_date DATETIME NOT NULL, location VARCHAR(100) NOT NULL, quota INT NOT NULL, status VARCHAR(20) NOT NULL);
CREATE TABLE admin (admin_id INT AUTO_INCREMENT PRIMARY KEY, full_name VARCHAR(100) NOT NULL, role VARCHAR(30) NOT NULL, email VARCHAR(100) NOT NULL UNIQUE);
CREATE TABLE registration (
  registration_id INT AUTO_INCREMENT PRIMARY KEY, nim VARCHAR(15) NOT NULL, workshop_id INT NOT NULL,
  registered_at DATETIME NOT NULL, status VARCHAR(20) NOT NULL,
  CONSTRAINT uq_reg UNIQUE (nim, workshop_id),
  FOREIGN KEY (nim) REFERENCES student(nim), FOREIGN KEY (workshop_id) REFERENCES workshop(workshop_id));
CREATE TABLE attendance (
  attendance_id INT AUTO_INCREMENT PRIMARY KEY, registration_id INT NOT NULL UNIQUE, admin_id INT NULL,
  checked_in_at DATETIME NOT NULL, status VARCHAR(20) NOT NULL, is_verified BOOLEAN NOT NULL DEFAULT FALSE,
  FOREIGN KEY (registration_id) REFERENCES registration(registration_id) ON DELETE CASCADE,
  FOREIGN KEY (admin_id) REFERENCES admin(admin_id));
CREATE TABLE material (material_id INT AUTO_INCREMENT PRIMARY KEY, workshop_id INT NOT NULL, title VARCHAR(150) NOT NULL, file_url VARCHAR(255) NOT NULL, uploaded_at DATETIME NOT NULL,
  FOREIGN KEY (workshop_id) REFERENCES workshop(workshop_id) ON DELETE CASCADE);
```

## 14. STATE MODELS & BUSINESS RULES

```mermaid
stateDiagram-v2
  state Workshop.status { [*] --> OPEN; OPEN --> ONGOING; ONGOING --> CLOSED }
  state Attendance { [*] --> PRESENT_UNVERIFIED: saveAttendance; PRESENT_UNVERIFIED --> VERIFIED: finalizeRecords; PRESENT_UNVERIFIED --> [*]: removed by admin }
```

Values `OPEN`, `ONGOING`, `present`, `isVerified` are from the report; `CLOSED` and `REGISTERED` (Registration.status) are **[PROPOSED]**.

Rules:
- **BR-1** registration only when `Workshop.status = OPEN`; attendance only when `ONGOING` (AD-SP-02 step A).
- **BR-2** NIM must exist/validate (`validateNIM`); invalid → `INVALID_NIM`.
- **BR-3** one Registration per (nim, workshop_id) → `DUPLICATE`; DB constraint is authoritative.
- **BR-4** one Attendance per Registration; repeat → `ALREADY_RECORDED`.
- **BR-5** new Attendance: `status="present"`, `is_verified=false`, `admin_id=NULL`.
- **BR-6** finalize runs verify → set `is_verified=true` + `admin_id` → update history, in **one transaction**.
- **BR-7** cancel finalization changes no data.
- **BR-8** quota enforcement is **undefined in the report**; implement behind a feature flag, default off [PROPOSED].
- **BR-9** pre-filled identity fields are read-only (Fig. 13 UI).

Error codes: `INVALID_NIM`, `DUPLICATE`, `NOT_REGISTERED`, `ALREADY_RECORDED`, `SESSION_NOT_ONGOING`, `NOT_FOUND`, `FORBIDDEN`.

## 15. KNOWN ISSUES IN THE SOURCE (resolve or ask; do not silently pick)

1. Author NIM: cover/table `245160407141003` vs Section 3 `245150407141003`.
2. Requirement IDs conflict between §3.4.2 (SR-01…07) and Tables 3.1/3.12/3.14 (SR-01…06, different meanings; STD-UR-04/05 vs 05/06). Use story/use-case IDs.
3. “Unmatched NIM” branch (UC-SP-08/09) is nearly unreachable because attendance requires a registration; keep as safeguard.
4. STD-FR-05 says materials need *verified attendance*; US-SP-05 says *registration confirmed*. Default: registration confirmed; make it a config switch.
5. Status enumerations and quota behavior undefined.

## 16. API CONTRACT (REST, JSON) [PROPOSED mapping of controller operations]

| Controller op | Method & path | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| requestPrefill | `GET /workshops/{id}/registration-form?nim=` | profile + history |
| processRegistration | `POST /workshops/{id}/registrations` | 201 / 422 `INVALID_NIM` / 409 `DUPLICATE` |
| requestHistory | `GET /students/{nim}/registrations` | |
| recordAttendance | `POST /workshops/{id}/attendance` `{nim}` | 201 / 404 `NOT_REGISTERED` / 409 `ALREADY_RECORDED` / 409 `SESSION_NOT_ONGOING` |
| getScheduleAndMaterials | `GET /workshops/{id}/materials?nim=` | 403/404 `NOT_REGISTERED` |
| requestDownload | `GET /materials/{id}/file` | |
| requestParticipationHistory | `GET /students/{nim}/participation` | registrations + attendance |
| requestPresentList | `GET /admin/workshops/{id}/attendance` | add SSE/WebSocket or polling for real time |
| updateEntry | `PATCH /admin/attendance/{id}` `{action}` | correct/remove |
| finalizeAttendance | `POST /admin/workshops/{id}/attendance/finalize` | uses authenticated admin_id |

Auth (UC-SP-01): student and admin sessions; admin routes require role check. Store NIM and attendance data securely (NFR-08): TLS, parameterized queries, least-privilege DB user, audit of finalization.

## 17. UI (low-fidelity, 4 screens)

1. Overview dashboard (CMMI 1 vs 2, 5-step workshop lifecycle).
2. Registration & central DB: NIM validation, pre-filled locked fields, duplicate check, participation history.
3. Live attendance: counters, NIM ingestion with instant roster match, roster cross-check, **Lock & Finalize**.
4. Schedules & materials: single repository, “Attendance Verified” badge, learning record, audit trail.

## 18. BUILD PLAN (do in this order, stop after each phase for review)

1. **Phase 0** — list assumptions & open questions (§15); confirm stack.
2. **Phase 1** — schema/migrations (§13), seed data, entity layer with the exact operations of §8.
3. **Phase 2** — RegistrationController + RD-SP-01/02 (UC-SP-02, 03, 10–12) + tests.
4. **Phase 3** — AttendanceController (UC-SP-04) + tests incl. concurrency on duplicates.
5. **Phase 4** — VerificationController (UC-SP-07/08/09/13) + real-time panel + transactional finalize.
6. **Phase 5** — MaterialController, ParticipationController, history pages.
7. **Phase 6** — auth, NFR-06…09 verification, load/lag check on admin panel.

## 19. OUTPUT FORMAT & DEFINITION OF DONE

For each phase output: (a) files changed, (b) code, (c) tests mapped to US/UC IDs, (d) a traceability line `US → UC → RD → SD → test`, (e) deviations flagged `[PROPOSED]`.

Done when: all acceptance criteria in §5 pass; every controller operation matches §8 names; BCE rules hold (no boundary→entity, no controller→actor calls); no extra domain tables exist; duplicate and double-attendance races are impossible at DB level; finalize is atomic.

**Self-check before replying:** Did I add a class not in §2.1? Did I rename a glossary term? Did an entity get called from a boundary? If yes, fix before answering